# Wave W17-N (Route 110): under turf — under-way meadow, a settled mid-green under the cycleway’s pillars with their long shadow flecks lying in it and the odd seed head standing (design: calm speckled grass under a raised cycling road, ponds and fence-lines in the grass beneath). Route 110’s own ground — deeper and more shadowed than Route 101’s young camp green, split by the pillar-shadow register.
